WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.820
I say this without exaggeration.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.250
I'm hooked on sugar.

3
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.230
I eat something sweet every single day, without exception.

4
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:13.520
At home we always have a stock of various sweets, and with a movie and snacks it has become almost a routine,

5
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.540
and sometimes I simply replace a whole meal with chocolate or cakes.

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.380
Sweets became something I ate without thinking.

7
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.530
If I have a honey-heart cookie or chocolate in the house, I'll take a piece no matter the time of day

8
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.100
and keep going back to them every little while as long as they're there.

9
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.160
If sweets or candy are served when visiting someone's house, you can be sure I'll try them.

10
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.460
If you offer me a slice of cake, it's unlikely that I'll turn it down.

11
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.420
And once I start, it's hard for me to stop.

12
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:50.200
Unless you live in a cave, by now you've already learned that too much added sugar is bad for you.

13
00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.520
Excessive sugar intake can cause obesity, diabetes, heart problems,

14
00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.500
affects immunity negatively, speeds up the aging process and causes cavities in your teeth

15
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.960
and it can also have a very bad effect on the look, texture and quality of your skin.

16
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.400
But probably the worst thing of all is one small detail that we most often avoid facing,

17
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.600
and that is that sugar is, in a way, a drug.

18
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.260
It's no secret that sugar is addictive, and the more we eat it, the more we need.

19
00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.800
However, as someone who has really experimented a lot with my diet in the past,

20
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:26.360
because I was a vegetarian, a vegan, a raw vegan, a keto vegan, a pescatarian,

21
00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.860
honestly, I got a little tired of reading all the labels and declarations on products

22
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.040
and counting every possible nutrient and the calories I take in.

23
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.080
The sugar addiction I picked up in the last few months

24
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.480
I didn't justify by the fact that, on top of treating myself to desserts every day,

25
00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.260
I didn't gain weight, or I'd tell myself: ah, okay, it's just chocolate, I'll do a workout later.

26
00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.740
However, the other symptoms started catching up with me.

27
00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.800
I started feeling listless and weak throughout the whole day, I had no focus,

28
00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.240
my energy level dropped significantly and my skin got worse.

29
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:09.080
All in all, I didn't feel great about myself and I knew that a lot of these things were a consequence of my diet.

30
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:15.600
That's why I decided to revise my eating and cut out one of the biggest enemies of my diet.

31
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.120
Added sugar.

32
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.760
The first step was to find everything I have in the house that contains added sugar and get rid of it.

33
00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.440
Okay, the rules are as follows.

34
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:31.660
No sweets, no snacks, not even salty ones, because believe it or not, they contain sugar too.

35
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.120
No dried fruit, no fruit juices, no fizzy drinks, no alcohol,

36
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.520
no sugar substitutes, like honey, agave syrup, maple syrup.

37
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.700
No artificial sweeteners, like aspartame, stevia.

38
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.140
Also no granola, no breakfast cereal.

39
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.500
And what's worst of all, no sugar in coffee.

40
00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.740
I decided to keep eating fruit, but with the caveat that I won't rely on it as my main source of energy,

41
00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.700
but I'll try to have a balanced diet.

42
00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.270
What will be the hardest part of this challenge for you?

43
00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:16.150
I have a habit after lunch, that is toward the evening, or after dinner, or sometimes even instead of dinner, of eating something sweet, so I think that's when I'll feel its absence the most.

44
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:21.740
So far I still feel totally okay, but my head started hurting around five or six,

45
00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:32.980
because even though I had breakfast, in that period between 12 and 5, when my energy drops, I usually grab and put in my mouth anything, a chocolate bar, a candy, something like that,

46
00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:41.570
but since I've restricted myself, I haven't eaten anything in between, right from breakfast on, and for lunch I've now made myself a salad.

47
00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.790
The first week was the hardest.

48
00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.430
I felt as if all my ships had sunk

49
00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:50.370
and I just wanted to cover myself with a blanket over my head and sleep through the whole day,

50
00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:55.210
hoping that tomorrow would be easier and that I'd be able to reap the fruits of my good decisions.

51
00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:01.910
The exhaustion and depression that appear as a consequence of abstaining from sugar are no joke,

52
00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.570
and if you even just try to do something like this,

53
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:09.490
I recommend that you clear your schedule so that you allow yourself as much time as possible

54
00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.490
for rest and relaxation during this challenging period.

55
00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.510
What I had to do was balance my diet.

56
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.770
I started cooking healthier meals with more greens,

57
00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.810
preparing a salad with every lunch, but also eating more.

58
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.070
All those calories that I used to take in through chocolate bars and snacks on the go,

59
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.690
I now had to make up for in a different way.

60
00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:45.290
Today I'm eating spaghetti with mushroom sauce and parmesan

61
00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.010
and this little salad that I made.

62
00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:59.370
The recommended daily sugar intake is 25 grams, which is equivalent to about 100 calories that should come from sugar.

63
00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.870
This adds up quite quickly.

64
00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:10.590
For example, some of my favourite sweets contain far more than the recommended daily intake, and that's in just one serving.

65
00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:14.490
Does this mean that we should completely eliminate all sugar from our diet?

66
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.590
Of course not, we just need to be careful.

67
00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:27.650
The main trick is to avoid processed food and base your diet on natural whole nutrients that come from fresh foods.

68
00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:35.570
You can also allow yourself some flexibility and have days with a high sugar intake, followed by days with a low sugar intake,

69
00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:44.250
however, what matters is that it balances out, say, on a weekly level, so that on average you took in 25 grams of sugar a day.

70
00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:47.850
One strange thing that happened, which I didn't expect,

71
00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:51.670
is that things that weren't sweet to me before

72
00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:52.890
have now become sweet.

73
00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:55.170
For example cheese, tomato, pepper.

74
00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.480
My palate somehow got cleansed

75
00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.630
and now I could feel their real taste.

76
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.460
Also, before it was absolutely unimaginable to me

77
00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.670
to drink coffee without sugar,

78
00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:07.330
however, when you cut out of your diet everything that contained sugar,

79
00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.470
you stop needing it,

80
00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.310
so even coffee wasn't bitter to me.

81
00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:17.630
I can't say that I don't crave sweets at all, although it's much easier for me than I thought it would be.

82
00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:28.150
I most feel like eating in the evening, somewhere around 6 to 7, even 8, late like that, after dinner, where I hadn't imposed this block and this ban on myself.

83
00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:33.370
I would probably have gone to the shop to buy something sweet, some chocolate bar, a honey heart, whatever.

84
00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:39.990
I started eating a lot more regular food, healthy food, and more in terms of quantity, even more often.

85
00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:45.680
What also helps me a lot is sparkling water; I never used to have a habit of drinking sparkling water,

86
00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:52.210
but since I cut out sugar, I really feel like drinking sparkling water, so I drink it every day and always keep it in the fridge.

87
00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:58.270
Typically, my cravings for sweets would appear out of boredom, sadness or a wish to celebrate something.

88
00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:05.430
Still, most often the urge for something sweet came in the evening, because that's the time when my body asks for some extra energy,

89
00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:09.430
but I learned to suppress those urges and tea helped me a lot with that.

90
00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:15.430
In the evening I'd make myself a cup of chamomile or mint tea and that would cut off my sudden craving for chocolate.

91
00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:19.730
I also replaced snacks with far healthier options.

92
00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:25.030
Today for lunch we have falafel, asparagus and salad.

93
00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.870
Honestly, I feel really bad today.

94
00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:35.650
I feel my head is about to start hurting and I imagine it's because I'm either dehydrated or something like that.

95
00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:40.350
Today is definitely one of the harder days and honestly I can't wait for this challenge to end.

96
00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:46.950
On the positive side, I'm really pleased with how my face has recovered in the last few weeks.

97
00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:52.670
I had one pimple here, but I have no more serious inflammation on my face at all.

98
00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.410
Honestly, I'm very happy about that.

99
00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:59.890
After a month of abstaining from sugar, I'm happy to be able to report

100
00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.110
that the results were mostly positive.

101
00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:08.430
I felt more productive, I had more vigour and my energy level was more constant throughout the day.

102
00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:12.010
My focus was better and my mood improved.

103
00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:17.930
I lost one kilogram, but I felt much stronger and more satisfied than a month ago.

104
00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:26.350
And so, after everything, in the end, I'm definitely glad that I did this challenge

105
00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:32.610
and I learned a lot of things about myself, about the food I eat, when it comes to desserts and sweets.

106
00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:36.590
I love them and I don't plan to give them up completely.

107
00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:40.770
However, this challenge definitely taught me that I need to pull the brake sometimes

108
00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:44.790
and go back to consuming certain foods in moderation

109
00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:49.310
and that I shouldn't really give in at every urge of my body for something sweet,

110
00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:52.490
but that I should sometimes turn to some healthier options.

111
00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:54.950
One big lesson that I learned from all of this

112
00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:59.490
is that I have to be much more careful about what I put into my body,

113
00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:08.170
because the food sold, say, in supermarkets is made primarily to be tasty, which doesn't mean it's good for us.

114
00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:13.200
Tell me what you think about all of this and whether you've ever done something similar,

115
00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:18.030
whether you dare to measure how much sugar a day you take in through your diet.

116
00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.590
Write me your opinion in the comments below.

117
00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:25.010
And of course, don't forget to like this video if you enjoyed it, it would mean a lot to me.

118
00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.150
and if you haven't yet, subscribe to my channel.

119
00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:32.390
That would be all for today, I send you lots of kisses and see you in one of the next videos.
